# Poddy workspace SSH policy.
#
# This file is installed as /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-poddy.conf. OpenSSH reads
# sshd_config.d from the Include at the top of the distribution config and keeps
# the first value for each option, so these settings override the distro
# defaults (notably UsePAM yes).
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
PermitRootLogin no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
AuthorizedKeysFile .ssh/authorized_keys
UsePAM no
UseDNS no
GSSAPIAuthentication no
HostbasedAuthentication no
X11Forwarding no
PermitTunnel no
GatewayPorts no
MaxAuthTries 3
LoginGraceTime 30
ClientAliveInterval 30
ClientAliveCountMax 3
AllowUsers dev
LogLevel VERBOSE
